{"headword":"שָׂבֵעַ","parent_lexicon":"BDB Dictionary","content":{"senses":[{"definition":"<strong>vb.</strong> be sated, satisfied, surfeited <strong>(</strong>NH (der. spec.) = BH; so Assyrian <em>šebû</em>, Arabic <span dir=\"rtl\">شَبِعَ</span>, Aramaic <span dir=\"rtl\">סְבַע</span>, <span dir=\"rtl\">ܣܒܰܥ</span>, Palm. <span dir=\"rtl\">שבע</span>; the Ethiopic vb. of same meaning is ጸግበ: <strong>)</strong>;—"},{"senses":[{"definition":"Pf. 3 ms. <span dir=\"rtl\">שָׂבַע</span> <a data-ref=\"I Chronicles 23:1\" href=\"/I_Chronicles.23.1\">1 Ch 23:1</a>, <span dir=\"rtl\">וְשׂ׳</span> consec. <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 31:20\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.31.20\">Dt 31:20</a>; 3 pl. <span dir=\"rtl\">שָׂבֵ֑עוּ</span> <a data-ref=\"Isaiah 9:19\" href=\"/Isaiah.9.19\">Is 9:19</a>, <span dir=\"rtl\">ושׂ׳</span> consec. <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 14:29\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.14.29\">Dt 14:29</a>; <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 26:12\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.26.12\">26:12</a>, etc.; Impf. 3 ms. <span dir=\"rtl\">יִשְׂבַּע</span> <a data-ref=\"Proverbs 12:11\" href=\"/Proverbs.12.11\">Pr 12:11</a> +, 3 mpl. <span dir=\"rtl\">יִשְׂבְּעוּן</span> <a data-ref=\"Psalms 104:28\" href=\"/Psalms.104.28\">ψ 104:28</a>, etc.; Imv. <span dir=\"rtl\">שְׂבַע־</span> <a data-ref=\"Proverbs 20:13\" href=\"/Proverbs.20.13\">Pr 20:13</a>; Inf. abs. <span dir=\"rtl\">שָׂבוֹעַ</span> <a data-ref=\"Joel 2:26\" href=\"/Joel.2.26\">Jo 2:26</a> <a data-ref=\"II Chronicles 31:10\" href=\"/II_Chronicles.31.10\">2 Ch 31:10</a>; cstr. <span dir=\"rtl\">לִשְׂבֹּעַ</span> <a data-ref=\"Exodus 16:8\" href=\"/Exodus.16.8\">Ex 16:8</a> <a data-ref=\"Lamentations 5:6\" href=\"/Lamentations.5.6\">La 5:6</a>, <span dir=\"rtl\">לְשָׂבְעָה</span> <a data-ref=\"Haggai 1:6\" href=\"/Haggai.1.6\">Hg 1:6</a>;—"},{"senses":[{"definition":"<em>be sated</em> (with food), especially human subj.:"},{"senses":[{"definition":"abs., after <span dir=\"rtl\">אָכַל</span>, <a data-ref=\"Hosea 4:10\" href=\"/Hosea.4.10\">Ho 4:10</a>; <a data-ref=\"Isaiah 9:19\" href=\"/Isaiah.9.19\">Is 9:19</a>; <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 8:10\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.8.10\">Dt 8:10</a>; <a data-ref=\"Exodus 16:8\" href=\"/Exodus.16.8\">Ex 16:8</a> (P), + 11 times, cf. <a data-ref=\"Isaiah 44:16\" href=\"/Isaiah.44.16\">Is 44:16</a> (‖ <span dir=\"rtl\">אָכַל</span>); exposing men to arrogance <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 6:11\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.6.11\">Dt 6:11</a>; <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 8:12\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.8.12\">8:12</a>; <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 31:20\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.31.20\">31:20</a>, cf. <a data-ref=\"Hosea 13:6\" href=\"/Hosea.13.6\">Ho 13:6</a><sup>(×2)</sup> (Isr. under fig. of cattle), <a data-ref=\"Jeremiah 50:19\" href=\"/Jeremiah.50.19\">Je 50:19</a> (id.; c. ב loc.; ‖ <span dir=\"rtl\">רָעָה</span> <em>graze</em>); = have (or get) enough to eat <a data-ref=\"Psalms 37:19\" href=\"/Psalms.37.19\">ψ 37:19</a>; <a data-ref=\"Psalms 59:16\" href=\"/Psalms.59.16\">59:16</a>, enough to drink <a data-ref=\"Amos 4:8\" href=\"/Amos.4.8\">Am 4:8</a>, fig. of sword <a data-ref=\"Jeremiah 46:10\" href=\"/Jeremiah.46.10\">Je 46:10</a>, of wine <a data-ref=\"Habakkuk 2:5\" href=\"/Habakkuk.2.5\">Hb 2:5</a>."}],"num":"a."},{"senses":[{"definition":"c. acc. of food <a data-ref=\"Jeremiah 44:17\" href=\"/Jeremiah.44.17\">Je 44:17</a>; <a data-ref=\"Lamentations 5:6\" href=\"/Lamentations.5.6\">La 5:6</a>; <a data-ref=\"Exodus 16:12\" href=\"/Exodus.16.12\">Ex 16:12</a> (P), + 6 times, cf. <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 39:20\" href=\"/Ezekiel.39.20\">Ez 39:20</a> (of beasts, in fig.), of earth, sated with water (rain) <a data-ref=\"Proverbs 30:16\" href=\"/Proverbs.30.16\">Pr 30:16</a>, so of trees (acc. om.) <a data-ref=\"Psalms 104:16\" href=\"/Psalms.104.16\">ψ 104:16</a>, fig. of requital <a data-ref=\"Proverbs 18:20\" href=\"/Proverbs.18.20\">Pr 18:20b</a>."}],"num":"b."},{"senses":[{"definition":"c. <span dir=\"rtl\">מִן</span> of food <a data-ref=\"Job 19:22\" href=\"/Job.19.22\">Jb 19:22</a> (fig.); fig. of earth having its fill (of rain) <a data-ref=\"Psalms 104:13\" href=\"/Psalms.104.13\">ψ 104:13</a>, and (fig. of requital) <a data-ref=\"Proverbs 18:20\" href=\"/Proverbs.18.20\">Pr 18:20a</a>; good sense <a data-ref=\"Proverbs 12:14\" href=\"/Proverbs.12.14\">12:14</a> (del. <span dir=\"rtl\">טוֹב</span>, so Toy), bad sense <a data-ref=\"Proverbs 1:31\" href=\"/Proverbs.1.31\">1:31</a>; <a data-ref=\"Proverbs 14:14\" href=\"/Proverbs.14.14\">14:14</a>; c. <span dir=\"rtl\">מִן</span> of source <a data-ref=\"Isaiah 66:11\" href=\"/Isaiah.66.11\">Is 66:11</a> (fig.)."}],"num":"c."}],"num":"1."},{"senses":[{"definition":"more gen., <em>be sated</em>, have desire satisfied:"},{"senses":[{"definition":"abs. <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 16:28\" href=\"/Ezekiel.16.28\">Ez 16:28</a>, <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 16:29\" href=\"/Ezekiel.16.29\">29</a> (i.e. with harlotry), <a data-ref=\"Jeremiah 50:10\" href=\"/Jeremiah.50.10\">Je 50:10</a> (with plunder), <a data-ref=\"Isaiah 53:11\" href=\"/Isaiah.53.11\">Is 53:11</a> (with a given result); of eyes <a data-ref=\"Proverbs 27:20\" href=\"/Proverbs.27.20\">Pr 27:20</a>, of Sh<sup>e</sup>ʾôl and Abaddōn v <a data-ref=\"Proverbs 27:20\" href=\"/Proverbs.27.20\">20</a>, cf. <a data-ref=\"Proverbs 30:15\" href=\"/Proverbs.30.15\">30:15</a>; = have abundance <a data-ref=\"Proverbs 30:9\" href=\"/Proverbs.30.9\">Pr 30:9</a> (exposure to arrogance)."}],"num":"a."},{"senses":[{"definition":"c. acc., <em>be satisfied with, have one’s fill of:</em> <a data-ref=\"Jeremiah 31:14\" href=\"/Jeremiah.31.14\">Je 31:14</a>, cf. <a data-ref=\"Psalms 17:15\" href=\"/Psalms.17.15\">ψ 17:15</a>; <a data-ref=\"Psalms 63:6\" href=\"/Psalms.63.6\">63:6</a>;<a data-ref=\"Proverbs 5:10\" href=\"/Proverbs.5.10\">Pr 5:10</a>; <a data-ref=\"Ecclesiastes 5:9\" href=\"/Ecclesiastes.5.9\">Ec 5:9</a>, cf. (eye subj.) <a data-ref=\"Ecclesiastes 4:8\" href=\"/Ecclesiastes.4.8\">4:8</a>, acc. of sons <a data-ref=\"Psalms 17:14\" href=\"/Psalms.17.14\">ψ 17:14</a> (si vera l., but text dub., v. Ol Du, cf. Bae We), days of life, i.e. reach the full limit (+ <span dir=\"rtl\">זָקֵן</span>) <a data-ref=\"I Chronicles 23:1\" href=\"/I_Chronicles.23.1\">1 Ch 23:1</a>; <a data-ref=\"II Chronicles 24:15\" href=\"/II_Chronicles.24.15\">2 Ch 24:15</a>."}],"num":"b."},{"senses":[{"definition":"c. ב of goodness <a data-ref=\"Psalms 65:5\" href=\"/Psalms.65.5\">ψ 65:5</a>, c. <span dir=\"rtl\">מִן</span> id. <a data-ref=\"Ecclesiastes 6:3\" href=\"/Ecclesiastes.6.3\">Ec 6:3</a>."}],"num":"c."},{"senses":[{"definition":"c. ל inf., <span dir=\"rtl\">לֹא־תִשְׂבַּע עַיִן לִרְאוֹת</span> <a data-ref=\"Ecclesiastes 1:8\" href=\"/Ecclesiastes.1.8\">Ec 1:8</a> (‖ <span dir=\"rtl\">מָלֵא</span>)."}],"num":"d."}],"num":"2."},{"senses":[{"definition":"<em>have in excess, be surfeited with:</em>"},{"senses":[{"definition":"lit., with honey (acc.) <a data-ref=\"Proverbs 25:16\" href=\"/Proverbs.25.16\">Pr 25:16</a>."}],"num":"a."},{"senses":[{"definition":"fig. = <em>be weary of</em>, c. acc. of offerings <a data-ref=\"Isaiah 1:11\" href=\"/Isaiah.1.11\">Is 1:11</a> (subj. <span dir=\"rtl\">י׳</span>), tossings <a data-ref=\"Job 7:4\" href=\"/Job.7.4\">Jb 7:4</a>, poverty <a data-ref=\"Proverbs 28:19\" href=\"/Proverbs.28.19\">Pr 28:19</a>, shame <a data-ref=\"Habakkuk 2:16\" href=\"/Habakkuk.2.16\">Hb 2:16</a>, contempt <a data-ref=\"Psalms 123:3\" href=\"/Psalms.123.3\">ψ 123:3</a>, <a data-ref=\"Psalms 123:4\" href=\"/Psalms.123.4\">4</a>, c. acc. pers. <a data-ref=\"Proverbs 25:17\" href=\"/Proverbs.25.17\">Pr 25:17</a>."}],"num":"b."},{"senses":[{"definition":"id., c. ב of troubles <a data-ref=\"Psalms 88:4\" href=\"/Psalms.88.4\">ψ 88:4</a>, of reproach <a data-ref=\"Lamentations 3:30\" href=\"/Lamentations.3.30\">La 3:30</a>."}],"num":"c."}],"num":"3."}],"occurrences":"79","form":"Qal"},{"senses":[{"definition":"Pt. <span dir=\"rtl\">נִשְׂבָּע</span> <em>sated</em> <a data-ref=\"Job 31:31\" href=\"/Job.31.31\">Jb 31:31</a>."}],"all_cited":true,"form":"Niph."},{"senses":[{"definition":"<em>satisfy</em>, Impf. 3 mpl. <span dir=\"rtl\">יְשַׂבֵּ֑עוּ</span> <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 7:19\" href=\"/Ezekiel.7.19\">Ez 7:19</a> <em>they shall</em> not <em>satisfy</em> their appetite (<span dir=\"rtl\">נֶפֶשׁ</span>; ‖ <span dir=\"rtl\">מִלֵּא</span>); Imv. ms. sf., subj. <span dir=\"rtl\">י׳</span>, <span dir=\"rtl\">שַׂבְּעֵנוּ חַסְדֶּ֑ךָ</span> <a data-ref=\"Psalms 90:14\" href=\"/Psalms.90.14\">ψ 90:14</a> (2 acc.)."}],"all_cited":true,"form":"Pi."},{"senses":[{"definition":"Pf. 3 ms. <span dir=\"rtl\">הִשְׂבִּיעַ</span> <a data-ref=\"Psalms 107:9\" href=\"/Psalms.107.9\">ψ 107:9</a>, <span dir=\"rtl\">וְה׳</span> consec. <a data-ref=\"Isaiah 58:11\" href=\"/Isaiah.58.11\">Is 58:11</a>; 2 fs. <span dir=\"rtl\">הִשְׂבַּ֫עַתְּ</span> <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 27:33\" href=\"/Ezekiel.27.33\">Ez 27:33</a>, etc.; Impf. 3 ms. sf. <span dir=\"rtl\">יַשְׂבִּעַנִי</span> <a data-ref=\"Job 9:18\" href=\"/Job.9.18\">Jb 9:18</a>, 2 ms. <span dir=\"rtl\">תַּשְׂבִּיעַ</span> <a data-ref=\"Isaiah 58:10\" href=\"/Isaiah.58.10\">Is 58:10</a>, 1 s. <span dir=\"rtl\">וָאַשְׂבִּעַ</span> <a data-ref=\"Jeremiah 5:7\" href=\"/Jeremiah.5.7\">Je 5:7</a>, sf. <span dir=\"rtl\">אַשְׂבִּיעֶ֑ךָּ</span> <a data-ref=\"Psalms 81:17\" href=\"/Psalms.81.17\">ψ 81:17</a> van d. H., <span dir=\"rtl\">אַשְׂבִּיעֶ֑ךָֿ</span> Baer Gi, etc.; Inf. cstr. <span dir=\"rtl\">לְהַשְׂבִּיעַ</span> <a data-ref=\"Job 38:27\" href=\"/Job.38.27\">Jb 38:27</a>; Pt. <span dir=\"rtl\">מַשְׂבִּיעַ</span> <a data-ref=\"Psalms 103:5\" href=\"/Psalms.103.5\">ψ 103:5</a>; <a data-ref=\"Psalms 145:16\" href=\"/Psalms.145.16\">145:16</a>;—"},{"senses":[{"senses":[{"definition":"<em>satisfy</em> (especially with material blessings), subj. <span dir=\"rtl\">י׳</span>, c. acc. pers. <a data-ref=\"Jeremiah 5:7\" href=\"/Jeremiah.5.7\">Je 5:7</a> (exposing men to arrogance), <a data-ref=\"Isaiah 58:11\" href=\"/Isaiah.58.11\">Is 58:11</a> (acc. <span dir=\"rtl\">נֶפֶשׁ</span>; of refreshment in drought, ב loc., fig. of help and blessing), <a data-ref=\"Psalms 107:9\" href=\"/Psalms.107.9\">ψ 107:9</a> (acc. <span dir=\"rtl\">נֶפֶשׁ</span>; ‖ <span dir=\"rtl\">מִלֵּא</span>), cf. <a data-ref=\"Psalms 103:5\" href=\"/Psalms.103.5\">103:5</a> (<span dir=\"rtl\">ב</span> instr., on acc. v. <a data-ref=\"BDB, עֲדִי\" href=\"/BDB,_עֲדִי\", dir=\"rtl\">עֲדִי</a>); c. acc. of ground <a data-ref=\"Job 38:27\" href=\"/Job.38.27\">Jb 38:27</a> (i.e. with rain); human subj., c. acc. <span dir=\"rtl\">נֶפֶשׁ</span> <a data-ref=\"Isaiah 58:10\" href=\"/Isaiah.58.10\">Is 58:10</a>."}],"num":"a."},{"senses":[{"definition":"c. acc. of food + pers., <span dir=\"rtl\">י׳</span> subj., <a data-ref=\"Psalms 81:17\" href=\"/Psalms.81.17\">ψ 81:17</a> (‖ <span dir=\"rtl\">הֶאֱכִיל</span>), <a data-ref=\"Psalms 105:40\" href=\"/Psalms.105.40\">105:40</a>; <a data-ref=\"Psalms 132:15\" href=\"/Psalms.132.15\">132:15</a>; <a data-ref=\"Psalms 147:14\" href=\"/Psalms.147.14\">147:14</a>; c. acc. pers. + <span dir=\"rtl\">אֹרֶךְ יָמִים</span> <a data-ref=\"Psalms 91:16\" href=\"/Psalms.91.16\">91:16</a>."}],"num":"b."},{"senses":[{"definition":"<span dir=\"rtl\">י׳</span> subj., acc. rei + ל pers., <span dir=\"rtl\">מַשׂ׳ לְכָל־חַי רָצוֹן</span> <a data-ref=\"Psalms 145:16\" href=\"/Psalms.145.16\">ψ 145:16</a>."}],"num":"c."},{"senses":[{"definition":"<span dir=\"rtl\">י׳</span> subj., c. acc. of beasts + <span dir=\"rtl\">מִמְּךָ</span> (of Pharaoh, in prophetic fig.) <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 32:4\" href=\"/Ezekiel.32.4\">Ez 32:4</a>."}],"num":"d."}],"num":"1."},{"senses":[{"definition":"<em>enrich</em>, subj. Tyre, c. acc. gent. <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 27:33\" href=\"/Ezekiel.27.33\">Ez 27:33</a> (‖ <span dir=\"rtl\">הֶעֱשִׁיר</span>)."}],"num":"2."},{"senses":[{"definition":"<em>sate, glut</em> (with the undesired), subj. <span dir=\"rtl\">י׳</span>, c. acc. pers. + ב rei <a data-ref=\"Lamentations 3:15\" href=\"/Lamentations.3.15\">La 3:15</a>, acc. pers. + rei <a data-ref=\"Job 9:18\" href=\"/Job.9.18\">Jb 9:18</a>."}],"num":"3."}],"all_cited":true,"form":"Hiph."}]},"rid":"BDB09600","strong_numbers":["7649","7646"],"next_hw":"שֹׂ֫בַע","prev_hw":"שְׂבָם","brackets":"first_word","alt_headwords":[{"word":"שָׂבַע"},{"word":"","occurences":"96"}],"root":true,"quotes":[],"GK":["8428","8425"],"TWOT":["2231d","2231"],"parent_lexicon_details":{"name":"BDB Dictionary","language":"heb.biblical","to_language":"eng","text_categories":[],"source":"BDB Dictionary","attribution":"F. Brown, S. Driver & C. Briggs","index_title":"BDB","version_title":"A Hebrew and English lexicon of the Old Testament, by Francis Brown. With the co-operation of S. R. Driver and Charles A. Briggs. Oxford, 1906","version_lang":"en","should_autocomplete":true}}